Generic single-database configuration.

**Not wired in yet, on purpose.** `seed.py` still uses
`Base.metadata.create_all()` to create tables - this migration (and
`alembic` itself, absent from `requirements.txt`) is deliberately parked
until the team is ready to switch, to avoid re-running a bug where two
people changed the table-creation strategy independently on diverged
branches. See `docs/plan-backend-securite.md` for the full context.

If you do turn this on: `alembic_version` is currently empty on every
existing database (since nothing has ever run `alembic upgrade head`
against it), so running it for the first time against a database that
`create_all()` already populated will fail with "table already exists".
Either `alembic stamp head` first, or start from a fresh database.
